Problem on Averages-11 - Placement Exercise
NOTE: This kind of question is very common in campus placement ( TCS, Wipro, etc.) because it makes the use of average and some basic logic.

Problem:
The average marks of 12 students in a class is 68. 
If the marks of two students are excluded, the average marks of the remaining 10 students becomes 65. 
If the marks of one of the excluded students is 72, find the marks obtained by the other student.

Solution:
Note: Formula of Average = Sum of observations / No. of observations.
Sum of observations = Averages X No. of observations.

Total marks of 12 students = 12 × 68 = 816

Total marks of remaining 10 students = 10 × 65 = 650

Total marks of the two excluded students = Total marks of 12 students - Total marks of remaining 10 students

Total marks of the two excluded students = 816 - 650 = 166

Marks of one excluded student = 72

Marks of the other excluded student = 166 - 72 = 94

Final Answer
👍 Marks obtained by the other student = 94
